FUN_1000_0a31 MEMMGR best-fit allocator + interlocking node-walk callees — faithful dynamic-DS/ES rewrite.

The Stage-1 gate (docs/stage1.md leg b). FUN_1000_0a31 is a best-fit allocator over a segment-linked
doubly-linked circular free list (control block at BP=param_5=DGROUP:0x16d4; node struct paragraph-based:
[0]=base,[2]=flags,[4]=size,[6]/[8]=owner off/seg,[0xc]=next-seg,[0xe]=prev-seg). At runtime DS/ES hold
node paragraphs and advance through node.next/prev each iteration; SS=DGROUP=0x1c00 so the ss:0xNN heap
bookkeeping (free-count 0x16dc, free-descriptor-list head 0x16e2, refill flag 0x1744, count 0x16da) is
DGROUP-absolute. Ghidra collapsed the walking DS/ES node fields into FIXED DGROUP globals
(DAT_1000_c004/c00c/c00e) -> constant re-read -> infinite spin (the rc=124 hang), and folded the
allocate/split path (0b1a/0b58/0b70) to *(int*)0x0 null-derefs. Reconstructed instruction-by-instruction
from the image (base-0 0x10a22..0x10bd0 + callees). Model: patches 013 (1467) / 015 (096c/0dc2).

The cooperating routines pass the current node through DS/ES across the near calls; __allregs does not
thread DS/ES, so they share an explicit cursor (the g_mm_* statics: g_mm_ds from patch 015 + g_mm_es/
g_mm_di/g_mm_bp/g_mm_ctl added here) and hand back CF/ZF the caller branches on. Rewritten faithfully:
  * 0a31 — refill-if-free-count<=3 (161d) -> primary size-walk -> best-fit search cascade
    (0bd1/0bef/0c21/0c7d/0c7f) -> split (0b1a) / exact-fit unlink (0b58) / finalize+sorted-insert (0b70).
    Returns AX = the allocated segment (descriptor.base) and leaves ES = the descriptor node for 184b.
  * 161d — descriptor-pool REFILL: bumps free-count so the recursive 184b->0a31 alloc doesn't re-refill,
    wraps the returned big block in a free node, then carves it into (size-1) new free descriptors.
  * 17e5 — allocate via 184b(struct DGROUP:0x1738); return the descriptor seg (AX) + CF; the decompile
    dropped the AX return and mis-based the DS seg to the static SS 0x2ba9 (runtime DS=DGROUP=0x1c00).
  * 0bd1/0bef/0c21/0c7d/0c7f — the ES/DS node-walk search helpers (0c7d = stc; 1040 = stc last-resort
    compaction stub). 0c21's deep block-relocating probe (1c68/1fcc) is NOT on the boot alloc path;
    it logs loudly and treats not-found (no silent heap corruption) if ever reached — like patch 015's
    0dc2 deep path.
  * 0d70 — unlink the current node from the doubly-linked list and reinsert/coalesce (1114).
  * 1110/1114 — sorted-insert + forward/backward coalesce of a freed node (FREE path; not the boot
    alloc path — the other 16 folded callers of 1110 need the same cursor treatment when free is
    exercised: documented follow-on).

